## Paper metadata (from arXiv abstract page)

- **arXiv id:** 2304.07917
- **Title:** Non-unitary Trotter circuits for imaginary time evolution
- **Authors:** Chiara Leadbeater, Nathan Fitzpatrick,
  David Mu\~noz Ramo, Alex J. W. Thom
- **Year:** 2023
- **Primary category:** quant-ph
- **Abstract (paraphrased):** proposes a Trotterised
  Probabilistic Imaginary-Time Evolution (PITE) scheme; each Pauli-string
  term in the qubit Hamiltonian is realised by a non-unitary version of
  the standard real-time Pauli gadget in which the ancilla is rotated by
  $R_x(\phi)$ with $\phi = 2\arccos(e^{-2|c_k|\Delta\tau})$ and mid-circuit
  measured; post-selecting the ancilla on $|0\rangle$ implements
  $\exp(-c_k \Delta\tau\,\sigma_k)$ up to a rescaling $\alpha$ (Eq. 26).
  Validated numerically on a 4-site TIM (Fig. 7) and a 2-site 1D Hubbard
  model (Fig. 8), with cumulative post-selection success probability
  reported vs.\ Trotter step.

